    slug: "structure-function-relationship-of-konjac-glucomannan-with-varying-acety-091c7083",
    titleZh: "魔芋葡甘聚糖在调节肠道菌群和缓解糖尿病前期中的作用",
    titleEn:
      "The Role of Konjac Glucomannan in Modulating Gut Microbiota and Alleviating Prediabetes",
    summaryZh:
      "为什么值得关注 糖尿病前期是一种血糖水平高于正常但不足以被归类为2型糖尿病的状态。 这是预防糖尿病发病的关键时期。 魔芋葡甘聚糖（KGM）被认为有助于糖尿病管理，但其结构如何影响其功能尚不清楚。",
    summaryEn:
      "Why it matters Prediabetes is a condition characterized by elevated blood glucose levels, offering a critical window for diabetes prevention.",
    bodyZh:
      "为什么值得关注 糖尿病前期是一种血糖水平高于正常但不足以被归类为2型糖尿病的状态。 这是预防糖尿病发病的关键时期。 魔芋葡甘聚糖（KGM）被认为有助于糖尿病管理，但其结构如何影响其功能尚不清楚。\n\n证据告诉我们什么 研究发现，乙酰化度（DS）较高的魔芋葡甘聚糖在丰富有益肠道细菌和改善糖尿病前期条件下的葡萄糖和脂质代谢方面更为有效。\n\n应该怎样理解 研究结果强调了KGM的乙酰化度在调节肠道菌群中的重要性，这对糖尿病预防至关重要。 然而，该研究的局限性在于其侧重于动物模型和体外实验。 需要更多的研究来证实这些效果在人类中是否成立。\n\n可以怎么做 对于糖尿病前期患者，考虑将富含魔芋葡甘聚糖的食物纳入您的饮食中，因为它可能有助于改善肠道健康和管理血糖水平。 这些发现为开发针对特定乙酰化度的KGM基础治疗药物提供了机会，以优化其在管理糖尿病前期和相关代谢状况中的效力。\n\n为什么和糖尿病前期有关？\n\n了解像魔芋葡甘聚糖这样的饮食成分如何影响肠道健康和代谢状况，对于为糖尿病前期和糖尿病开发有效的饮食和治疗干预措施至关重要。\n\n你可以带走的重点\n\n- 魔芋葡甘聚糖的结构，特别是其乙酰化度，在调节肠道菌群的能力中起着关键作用。\n- KGM中较高的乙酰化度与更好地丰富有益肠道细菌相关联。\n- 研究表明，在糖尿病前期条件下，DS较高的KGM可以改善葡萄糖和脂质代谢。\n- 需要更多的研究来证实这些发现在人类临床试验中的效果。",
    bodyEn:
      "Why it matters Prediabetes is a condition characterized by elevated blood glucose levels, offering a critical window for diabetes prevention.\n\nThe structure-function relationship of Konjac glucomannan (KGM) in diabetes management is not well understood.\n\nWhat the evidence says The study indicates that KGM with higher acetylation degrees (DS) enriches beneficial gut bacteria and improves glucose and lipid metabolism in prediabetic conditions.\n\nWhat this means The findings highlight the importance of KGM's acetylation degree in modulating gut microbiota, crucial for diabetes prevention.\n\nHowever, the reliance on animal models and in vitro experiments suggests the need for further human studies.\n\nWhat readers can do Incorporating KGM into diets may benefit prediabetic individuals by improving gut health and blood sugar levels.\n\nThere's potential for developing KGM-based therapeutics optimized for specific acetylation degrees.\n\nWhy This Matters for Prediabetes\n\nUnderstanding how dietary components like konjac glucomannan can influence gut health and metabolic conditions is crucial for developing effective dietary and therapeutic interventions for prediabetes and diabetes.\n\nPractical Takeaways\n\n- Konjac glucomannan's structure, specifically its acetylation degree, plays a crucial role in its ability to modulate gut microbiota.\n- Higher acetylation degrees in KGM were associated with better enrichment of beneficial gut bacteria.\n- The study suggests that KGM with higher DS can improve glucose and lipid metabolism in prediabetic conditions.\n- More research is needed to confirm these findings in human clinical trials.\n\n\n\n- Journal/source: PubMed prediabetes lifestyle intervention via PubMed (Carbohydrate polymers)\n- Evidence used: PubMed abstract + open-access full-text link\n- Original title: Structure-function relationship of Konjac glucomannan with varying acetylation degrees in modulating gut microbiota and alleviating prediabetes.\n- Authors: Wang H, Zhao Y, Dang D, Huang L, Pei Z, Zhao J et al.\n- PubMed: [https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41832011/](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41832011/)\n- DOI: [10.1016/j.carbpol.2026.125103](https://doi.org/10.1016/j.carbpol.2026.125103)\n\n- Open-access link: [https://doi.org/10.1016/j.carbpol.2026.125103](https://doi.org/10.1016/j.carbpol.2026.125103)\n- Published or indexed date: 2026-05-15\n\n如需阅读原文，请点击链接获取完整内容。\n\n本站文章基于公开学术文献进行第三方评论，不代表原文作者及出版机构立场。如涉版权问题，请权利人联系下架。",
