    titleZh: "连续葡萄糖监测与机器学习用于个性化代谢亚型分类",
    titleEn: "CGM and Machine Learning for Personalized Metabolic Subtyping",
    summaryZh: "原文信息栏",
    summaryEn:
      "Study Background Understanding early dysglycemia's complexity is crucial for diabetes prevention. Traditional methods using static glucose thresholds may not capture the full heterogeneity of metabolic dysfunctions.",
    bodyZh:
      "原文信息栏\n\n- Original title: Use of Continuous Glucose Monitoring With Machine Learning to Identify Metabolic Subphenotypes and Inform Precision Lifestyle Changes.\n- Authors: Metwally AA, Park H, Wu Y, McLaughlin T, Snyder MP\n- Journal/source: PubMed prediabetes lifestyle intervention via PubMed (Journal of diabetes science and technology)\n- DOI: [10.1177/19322968261431860](https://doi.org/10.1177/19322968261431860)\n- PubMed/source link: [https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41978474/](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41978474/)\n- Open-access link: [https://doi.org/10.1177/19322968261431860](https://doi.org/10.1177/19322968261431860)\n- Evidence used: PubMed abstract + open-access full-text link\n- Published or indexed date: 2026-05-01\n\n为什么值得关注 早期血糖异常的复杂性理解对于糖尿病预防至关重要。 传统使用静态血糖阈值的方法可能无法完全捕捉代谢功能障碍的异质性。\n\n证据告诉我们什么 连续葡萄糖监测（CGM）结合机器学习能预测肌肉胰岛素抵抗和β细胞功能。 个体对餐食的餐后血糖反应可以作为代谢亚型的生物标志物。\n\n应该怎样理解 利用CGM数据提供代谢健康的个性化视角。 它超越了一般的血糖控制，针对特定的代谢缺陷，这可能导致更有效的生活方式干预。 然而，技术的可及性和成本也可能是限制因素。\n\n可以怎么做 识别代谢亚型的能力可以通过允许定制的干预措施来彻底改变糖尿病预防。 这强调了将饮食、睡眠和体力活动等数据点整合到一个全面的代谢档案中的重要性。\n\n为什么和糖尿病前期有关？\n\n这项研究之所以相关，是因为它提供了管理糖尿病前期的新视角，并可能导致更有针对性的干预措施。 对于糖尿病前期患者来说，了解这些技术的潜在益处和局限性非常重要。\n\n你可以带走的重点\n\n- CGM和机器学习可以提供个性化的代谢档案。\n- 个体对食物的反应可以指示代谢亚型。\n- 精准的生活方式改变可能在糖尿病预防中更有效。\n- 该技术的实际应用和成本是考虑因素。",
    bodyEn:
      "Study Background Understanding early dysglycemia's complexity is crucial for diabetes prevention. Traditional methods using static glucose thresholds may not capture the full heterogeneity of metabolic dysfunctions.\n\nWhat the evidence says CGM combined with machine learning predicts muscle insulin resistance and beta-cell function. Individual postprandial glycemic responses to meals can indicate metabolic subtypes.\n\nWhat this means Leveraging CGM data offers a personalized metabolic health view. It targets specific metabolic defects, potentially leading to more effective lifestyle interventions.\n\nHowever, practical application and cost considerations are important.\n\nWhat readers can do Identifying metabolic subphenotypes could revolutionize diabetes prevention with tailored interventions.\n\nThis approach emphasizes the importance of integrating diet, sleep, and physical activity data into a comprehensive metabolic profile.\n\nWhy This Matters for Prediabetes\n\nThis study is relevant because it provides a new perspective on managing prediabetes and could lead to more targeted interventions.\n\nIt's important for those with prediabetes to understand the potential benefits and limitations of such technologies.\n\nPractical Takeaways\n\n- CGM and machine learning can offer personalized metabolic profiles.\n- Individual responses to food can indicate metabolic subtypes.\n- Precision lifestyle changes could be more effective in diabetes prevention.\n- Considerations include the technology's real-world application and cost.",
